-- migr:needs-session alter_column: MySQL has no statement that changes one attribute of a column: a type or nullability change is MODIFY COLUMN, a full redefinition, and every attribute it does not restate is dropped -- measured, a MODIFY of the type alone lost both the NOT NULL and the DEFAULT. Setting a default is the same statement whenever the column is a text, blob or json one, which ALTER COLUMN ... SET DEFAULT refuses outright with error 1101 on MySQL. So the attributes the operation does not name, and the column's type where it decides which default syntax is legal, are read from the database first
